From 86105f3cdabb163f20b724f549a16cd6fcbc3105 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guilherme Silva <239806034+NoneSilva@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:59:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH v1] fix(lm): bind the MCP server to loopback

The server called app.listen(port) with no host, so Node bound every
interface, and POST /mcp has no authentication. The server now binds the
host from a new setting, and the default is localhost. A client on
another machine now needs the setting set to an address outside loopback.

- tlaplus.mcp.host has scope machine. Only user or remote settings can
  change it, so the settings of a folder or a workspace cannot change the
  address. The description says that a value outside loopback puts the
  server on the network and that the server has no authentication. It
  says to set the host in the user settings of a local window or in the
  remote settings of a remote window, and that VS Code ignores a value in
  .vscode/settings.json.
- The server reads the setting itself, as it reads its other settings.
  A value that is not a non-empty string gives localhost. Node binds every
  interface for a host that is not a string, or is empty.
- When loopback has no IPv4, localhost binds ::1, because localhost can
  resolve to 127.0.0.1 alone. The name matches in any case, with or
  without a trailing dot. A machine that cannot list its interfaces, or
  lists no loopback, keeps localhost.
- The advertised URL names the address the server bound, so a client
  reaches that socket whatever its resolver prefers. A bind to 0.0.0.0 is
  advertised as 127.0.0.1. A bind to :: serves both families, so it is
  advertised as 127.0.0.1 too, or as [::1] when loopback has no IPv4.
  The log line also shows the bound address.
- Express 5 also calls the listen callback when the listen fails, and the
  callback logged a listening URL and registered it with VS Code and
  Cursor anyway. It now returns on an error, so no URL is registered, and
  the error handler reports the failure.
- Two tests that dialed 127.0.0.1 now dial the address the server bound.
  New tests cover the default bind, the name localhost at the bind, the
  host of the setting and its URL, a host outside loopback, the default,
  the scope and the description of the setting, a bind that fails on a
  held port or on an address that the machine does not have, the values
  of the setting that are not a non-empty string, the URL registered
  with VS Code, the URL of a bind to :: with and without IPv4 on
  loopback, the bind and the URL when loopback has no IPv4, and the
  advertised host of six binds. Tests with injected values cover the
  check of the loopback and an interface list that cannot be read.

A request that reaches the port with a foreign Host still gets an answer.

